# Per-run intermediates: the harness rewrites these every run, and they describe
# one machine's execution rather than the team's shared baseline. What belongs
# in git is the record — state.json, the reports, the run history, the outcome
# ledger, the profile — not the scratch a single run passed through.
facts.json
judgment.json
state.json.prev
run-in-progress.json
# Coverage intermediates. The harness writes these to a temp directory since
# 0.58.0; the names stay listed so a root that ran 0.53–0.57 cannot commit the
# 95 MB one it was left with (VERDICT-F-29).
coverage.rc
coverage.db
coverage.json
# test-ids.txt is tracked again (2026-10-15): it is the baseline the next run's id set-diff
# reads, and without it every fresh checkout saw all 2,731 tests as "added", so the sweep
# could never fire in team mode. The Claude directory reads the `directory` branch, which
# leaves .qa/ out, so its 256 KiB reader no longer sees this file.
